WEBVTT

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:04.600
Enter.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.800
Sir!

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.040
What can I do for you, sir?

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:17.010
I'm told your older brother
is also a Reasoner?

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.820
Yes, sir! He's stationed
on the Blanc Rouge,

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:22.590
a carrier in the 14th Mobile Fleet!

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.990
Why do you ask?

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:29.130
We've just learned that the Blanc Rouge
and the rest of the 14th Fleet

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:30.890
have been completely destroyed.

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:32.560
Huh?

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:38.400
They were at Planet Grabera when
the Deague made a surprise attack.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.900
Each ship fought back,
but it was in vain...

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.640
Grabera itself suffered
terrible destruction.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:48.810
And during the fighting, your brother...

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:53.420
No... My brother would never
lose to mere TUMORs...

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.520
No... the enemy was in a Strain.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:00.790
A Strain?! How do
the Deague have Strains?!

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:06.280
Ralph Werec, a Union Reasoner,
betrayed us!

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:19.740
My one and only dear brother
in the whole world...

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.580
My brother was everything to me...

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:26.820
My one and only dear brother
in the whole world...

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:33.820
I believed we would always...
always be able to be together...

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:38.160
Yet... Yet...

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.410
Sara...

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:16.240
Like Looking at Myself

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:25.330
You're Ralph Werec's
younger sister, Sara Werec.

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:27.630
Is that correct?

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:44.240
I'm gonna go work out.
I can't stand around like this.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:52.930
Could you start by telling
us about yourself?

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:59.260
Otherwise, we'll have to assume
that you're a Deague spy.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:03.100
I'm...

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.090
He's finally settled down...

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:24.860
Yes...

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:29.430
So many things have happened today...

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:31.260
Yeah...

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:39.870
It's all my fault... I'm so sorry...

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:45.710
I'm so sorry... I'm so sorry...
I'm so sorry...

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:51.810
Sara. Why did you use a false name
to enroll at this school?

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:58.520
Then allow me to change the question.

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:04.400
Why did you transfer here
in the guise of a Gambee pilot?

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:07.300
Because he destroyed it...

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:11.970
My brother destroyed my Mimic...

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:13.970
Then does your transfer here

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:21.480
have something to do with
Ralph Werec's attacks on this ship?

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.740
I don't know...

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:28.790
I want to know, too...

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:33.120
I want to know what my brother
is trying to do...

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.740
Such recklessness!

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:48.240
Ralph Werec! Leave the sample
here and stay in your quarters!

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:51.510
This latest incident means we can
no longer mount a surprise attack

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:54.010
after they've left port!

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:58.680
I'm going to restrain that sample
to keep it from doing this again!

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.550
It's been nothing but trouble...

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:04.010
I should've done this
from the very start!

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:13.560
W-why, you-

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:17.360
Don't touch her.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:38.220
Do you believe she's telling the truth?

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:40.460
It's too farfetched to be made up.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:45.060
Whatever the case, we will need to
continue our surveillance of her.

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.590
Yeah...

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:09.220
Immediate departure?! Please, wait!

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:12.220
We've only just begun our repairs!

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:14.430
I understand your situation.

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:18.430
However, you've already
been attacked by Ralph Werec

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:22.740
during sub-light speed travel,
a very unique situation in itself.

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:27.370
We can only assume this latest
attack was meant for you, as well.

00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:33.950
Very well. However, our ship
lacks sufficient facilities.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:37.350
May we at least leave
the severely injured with you?

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:41.420
--Of course.
--And one other thing...

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:45.960
We'll leave Sara Werec in your hands.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:49.930
There is a possibility she is secretly
communicating with the Deague.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:55.100
Handing her over to the Union outpost
here seems the most logical.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.570
I'm afraid we can't allow that.

00:06:57.570 --> 00:07:03.180
Orders from above. A Deague ship
is approaching here, you see...

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:05.240
A Deague ship?!

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:10.650
If their objective is
to recover Sara Werec...

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:13.490
...it would result in a battle here...

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:15.490
I'm grateful for your
swift understanding.

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:18.090
So you're just going to make us-

00:07:18.090 --> 00:07:23.860
You may say whatever you like.
So long as you leave port at once.

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:51.120
As I've stated many times,
we are running out of time.

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:57.030
After recalculation, if we don't
change course in 15 subjective hours,

00:07:57.030 --> 00:08:00.530
our ship will be unable to
rendezvous at the appointed time.

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:06.370
I'm aware of that! But there is
another sample on that ship!

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:10.310
Not to mention, you fully supported
Ralph's proposition yourself!

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:12.010
Only now you change your mind?!

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:16.720
Indeed, if his words are true,
it may turn the tide of the war.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:20.120
However, a different military
operation is waiting for us.

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:24.090
It is a certainty that should
we miss this rendezvous,

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:27.490
we will all be charged with crimes,
regardless of what gifts we bear!

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:28.630
But-

00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:32.460
I have no intention of
committing suicide with you!

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:37.370
Any more of this will prove
fatal for you, Captain.

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:40.570
Please think with a calm mind.

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:43.700
I cannot trust that man.

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:50.370
I will now prepare to change course.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:09.600
Take that, Ralph Werec!

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:15.240
This is... This is what you get for
ridiculing people! You damn kid!

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:19.450
I'm going to show you there's
no place in the Deague

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:21.000
for the likes of you!

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:43.440
She was actually a Deague spy?!

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:47.540
--Are you serious?!
--Yeah, everyone's talking about it!

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:50.810
Apparently, the attack
on Gall was her fault, too!

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:54.450
So that's why we're being kicked
out before our repairs are done!

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:58.820
Dammit! It's all that traitor's
fault everyone's being killed!

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:01.810
I don't want to die yet!

00:10:05.260 --> 00:10:08.660
Status report on the ship's repairs.

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:11.460
What's wrong?

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:13.930
The Deague ship is going
to come for her, isn't it?

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:15.570
"Her"?

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:21.370
There'd be no need for us to run
if we gave them Sara Werec, right?!

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:28.010
Even if that were the case,
there's no guarantee we'd be unharmed.

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:32.350
Besides, it hasn't been
determined that she is a spy.

00:10:32.350 --> 00:10:35.750
You should refrain from
making such careless remarks.

00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:37.990
Just have a little more patience.

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:40.960
There is a regular military
force at Planet Bregma

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:42.590
that helps conduct these exercises.

00:10:42.590 --> 00:10:45.930
Once there, a Deague ship
will be nothing to fear!

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:49.800
Now, then, everyone!
Prepare to leave port!

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.300
Lottie? It's me.

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:21.730
I brought you some food.
You should really eat a little...

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:23.390
Lottie?

00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:31.230
Lottie...

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:48.860
Course set to coordinates
NS-107W, Planet Bregma.

00:11:48.860 --> 00:11:53.700
Increasing engine output.
Mercurion level to 60%.

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:58.440
Lottie Gelh?

00:11:58.440 --> 00:11:59.740
What the-

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:01.740
What is she-

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:05.240
--Let us observe a bit.
--But-

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:09.080
She, if anyone, won't make a mistake.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:15.020
Eh? But...

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:16.890
Understood.

00:12:34.510 --> 00:12:36.370
Brother...

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:47.420
There is something I've decided to do.
No matter what it takes.

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:51.760
So... stay out of my way!

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:53.990
I won't show mercy to anyone
who gets in my way.

00:12:53.990 --> 00:12:57.430
Not even to you, Sara!

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:19.980
This is...

00:13:21.620 --> 00:13:24.620
--...Carris'...
--That's right.

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:27.260
It's a present.

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:32.860
From Carrisford, just before Ralph Werec,
your brother, killed him!

00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:49.780
It's not just Carrisford.

00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:55.720
Grabera, this exercise voyage...
Your brother has killed many people!

00:13:55.720 --> 00:14:00.660
But why are you still alive?!
Is it because you're his sister?!

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:04.660
How many more people
is he going to kill?!

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:07.630
How many until he's satisfied?!

00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:11.800
That traitor only makes piles
of corpses wherever he goes!

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:15.340
Do you have any idea how
many lives he's taken?!

00:14:15.340 --> 00:14:19.610
He's a specter of death who
only knows how to kill people!

00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:24.220
Listen! I'll never see my brother again!

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:28.920
I'll never see his face or touch him
or hear his voice ever again!

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:32.220
Yet, your brother is alive,
just fine and well!

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:36.560
Why, dammit?!
Say something, Sara Werec!

00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:44.940
Martha...

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:48.210
Have you seen Lottie?
She's not in her room...

00:14:48.210 --> 00:14:49.410
Nope...

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:53.970
Oh. Well, if you see her,
let me know right away.

00:14:56.780 --> 00:15:00.590
Damn it! Say something, Sara!

00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:02.950
I don't know...

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:05.490
I don't know what
happened to my brother...

00:15:05.490 --> 00:15:09.060
Or what he's trying to do...

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:12.530
I'm the one who wants to know...

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:14.430
I don't believe anything you say!

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:16.500
--I'm not lying!
--Shut up!

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:21.470
You lied about your name
and your past and everything else!

00:15:21.470 --> 00:15:26.750
But the only way to see my brother
again was to go to the front lines!

00:15:26.750 --> 00:15:28.380
I wanted to see him

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:33.550
and find out how he could
kill people so heartlessly!

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:38.590
I'm here now because I once
had a kind, gentle brother...

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:45.660
Without him, I wouldn't
have lived to today...

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:51.240
Without him... without him...

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:53.510
...I...

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:57.810
I... would've been all alone...

00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:28.940
After our parents died,
it was just me and my brother...

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:36.750
I was such a crybaby, but he always...
he always looked out for me.

00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:39.980
My brother was the only person I had...

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:44.620
On nights I felt so lonely
that I couldn't sleep,

00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:49.650
he would always stay by
my side until I fell asleep.

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:06.400
Before he left for the army,
I would fuss and say, "Don't go..."

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:22.330
At the time, I just couldn't
imagine being away from my brother.

00:17:22.330 --> 00:17:24.090
And then...

00:17:28.430 --> 00:17:31.500
--Ralph-oniichan!
--Sara!

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:34.010
Welcome home!

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:36.200
I'm home, Sara!

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:48.020
Being with my brother
was my happiness.

00:17:57.230 --> 00:18:04.100
So I thought it was only
natural to follow after him...

00:18:07.910 --> 00:18:09.740
Brother!

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:24.860
You're so silly, Lottie.
It's not like this is goodbye forever.

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:28.360
If you become a great Reasoner,
we'll share the same path.

00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:32.260
We'll meet again soon. Right?

00:18:34.570 --> 00:18:38.100
Yeah! Wait for me! I'm...

00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:39.940
I'm going to go!

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:43.170
--To where you'll be!
--To where you'll be!

00:18:43.170 --> 00:18:45.970
--Okay!
--I'll be waiting!

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:56.490
Only you can accomplish
what you've decided.

00:18:56.490 --> 00:19:01.360
As long as you believe in that,
there's surely nothing you can't do!

00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:09.290
Brother...

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:16.140
I... can't die...

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:20.850
I... won't let my brother kill any more.

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:22.910
That's what I've decided...

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:25.620
That's why...

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:27.690
...I'm...

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:32.650
...going to kill my brother myself!

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:37.460
Because I love him...

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:44.170
That's why I have
to kill my own brother...

00:19:44.170 --> 00:19:48.640
He's my one and only brother
in this world...

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:51.580
I won't let him kill anyone else!

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:34.370
The mystery behind Emily.
The truth of 600 years ago.

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:37.600
And the tragedy that
occurred in the future.

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:41.230
On the next Soukou no Strain:
"Memories of the Future"

00:20:41.230 --> 00:20:43.130
This is my brother's pain?
